+++ b/README.md
@@ -3,3 +3,24 @@
 A small TypeScript library, with no runtime dependency, of building blocks for our services that store,
 exchange and update JSON: configuration files, API payloads and stored records. It is imported by the
 other projects of the team, so its behaviour must follow the published standards it implements.
+
+## JSON Pointer
+
+`resolvePointer(document, pointer)` resolves a value in a JSON document using
+[RFC 6901 JSON Pointer](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6901). The empty
+pointer identifies the document itself. Each other pointer must start with `/`;
+its slash-separated reference tokens select object members or array elements.
+Within a token, `~1` denotes `/` and `~0` denotes `~`.
+
+```ts
+import { resolvePointer } from "json-toolkit";
+
+const document = { users: [{ name: "Ari" }], "a/b": { "~key": true } };
+
+resolvePointer(document, "/users/0/name"); // "Ari"
+resolvePointer(document, "/a~1b/~0key"); // true
+```
+
+The function throws when the pointer is malformed (including an invalid `~`
+escape), an array token is not a valid array index, or a selected member/index
+does not exist. It returns `JsonValue`, the exported type for JSON values.
